First if you install it as such, you will *only* be able to play nethack
with that user. I would suggest installing it as root to
/usr/games/nethack. Read the install instructions in the source code and
you'll soon find where it defines it. BTW you don't *need* to run X
every time you run linux, All you have to do is kill XDM and then exit
X11 (or your windowmanager - gnome kde etc.). And then if you don't
what it to run at *all* just starting it from a shell when you want
to run X- which you *can* in linux BTW,  - just like windows 3.1,
but with proper threading - you set it up to use startx instead of the
XDM daemon. Virtually *all* configuration in linux is done with straight
text files. There are exceptions, but you almost certainly won't need to
do anything like define your own character set for example.


http://tldp.org/HOWTO/XFree86-HOWTO/index.html

Somewhat dated, but you will probably find a current version in
/usr/doc/howto. 


